{# Rules & restrictions, one block per direction.

   The rules are folded to the strictest of the legs a direction flies, so what
   is listed holds for the whole journey rather than for its first flight. A
   restriction is marked as one — the point of the list is what the ticket will
   not let you do, and a bullet reads the same whichever way it falls. #}
<section class="rules" aria-labelledby="rules-heading">
    <h2 class="rules__heading" id="rules-heading">Rules &amp; restrictions</h2>

    {% for block in trip.rules %}
        <div class="rules__block">
            <p class="rules__route">
                Fare rules for {{ block.route }}
                <span class="rules__brand">{{ block.title }}</span>
            </p>
            <ul class="rules__list">
                {% for line in block.lines %}
                    <li class="rules__item{{ line.allowed ? '' : ' rules__item--restricted' }}">
                        <i class="fas {{ line.allowed ? 'fa-check' : 'fa-xmark' }} rules__icon"></i>
                        {{ line.text }}
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </div>
    {% endfor %}

    <ul class="rules__notes">
        <li>
            If you book a fare that allows changes, the airline may charge a change or cancel
            fee, plus any fare difference. Airlines set change and cancel policies and fee
            amounts. We may collect these change or cancel fees, which are then passed on to
            the airline.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Tickets are nonrefundable and nontransferable</strong> unless the fare says
            otherwise above. Name changes are not allowed.
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>
